\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Zero-overlap PFA cancellation and unified 3D conformal-recursive polar Cantor $(r, \theta , z)$ rotational clutch architecture (\texttt  {F3\_111}) in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Two-dimensional cross-sectional schematic comparing Euclidean parallel plates ($A_{\rm  overlap} > 0$, dominated by attractive proximity-force scaling $F_z^{\rm  PFA} \propto -A_{\rm  overlap}/d^4$), uniform periodic slot-tooth interdigitation ($A_{\rm  overlap} = 0$, limited by single-scale evanescent screening at $\kappa \sim \pi /W_0$), and unified 3D prefractal Cantor interdigitation ($U=(1,1,1)$ in $(r,\theta ,z)$, with radial sub-slots $W_k = W_1 b^{-(k-1)}$, azimuthal Cantor lobe sub-apertures, and stepped vertical depths $H_m \in \{90, 80, 70\}\text  { nm}$ partitioning transverse fringing fields across separated wavenumber sub-bands). \textbf  {b}, Three-dimensional cutaway render of the optimal unified 3D polar Cantor clutch (\texttt  {F3\_111}, $C_4$ symmetry, $90^\circ $ sector period, $R \in [0.3{}, 1.65{}]\ \mu \text  {m}$) in the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $). In each $90^\circ $ sector, $12$ radial rotor sub-teeth split azimuthally into $24$ stepped 3D Cantor lobes ($96$ lobes total across all four sectors; colour-coded by prefractal generation in Sector~$0$ as gold $m=1$ [$H_1 = 90\text  { nm}$], orange $m=2$ [$H_2 = 80\text  { nm}$], and coral $m=3$ [$H_3 = 70\text  { nm}$]) interdigitate inside $12$ Cantor stator sub-slots bounded by $8$ primary gold stator ribs and $5$ internal copper-gold Cantor stator sub-ribs ($25\text  { nm}$ membrane thickness, $z \in [-25, 0]\text  { nm}$) suspended above recessed azimuthal landing pads ($150\text  { nm}$ thickness, top surface at $z_{\rm  pad,top} = -115\text  { nm}$) and supported by a twin-forked single-crystal $\text  {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ spider suspension. \textbf  {c},\textbf  {d}, Cutaway renders and axial-radial $(r,z)$ cross-sections of \texttt  {F3\_111} in (\textbf  {c}) the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $, $A_{\rm  overlap} = 0$, $F_z^{\rm  PFA} = 0$, showing upward saddle-point repulsive force $F_z = +\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ and areal density $\roundtwo  {60.8337}\text  { pN}\,\mu \text  {m}^{-2}$ across the stepped tips $z_{{\rm  tip},m} \in \{-90, -80, -70\}\text  { nm}$, remaining repulsive at $+\roundtwo  {2.88865}\text  { pN}$ at the $\theta = 21^\circ $ straddling transition) and (\textbf  {d}) the engaged landing-pad state ($\theta = 48^\circ $, $A_{\rm  overlap} = \roundthree  {0.304944}\ \mu \text  {m}^2$ across the stepped vertical gaps $d_m \in \{25, 35, 45\}\text  { nm}$ above $z_{\rm  pad,top} = -115\text  { nm}$, switching to strong normal attraction $F_z = \roundtwo  {-19.9798}\text  { pN}$). \textbf  {e}, Six-stage radial cross-sectional progression across $r \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text  {m}$ from the single-track baseline ($N=0$, $+\roundtwo  {0.7067}\text  { pN}$), three-track uniform grating ($+\roundtwo  {1.19524}\text  { pN}$), and stepped $(r,z)$ $N=2$ Cantor ring ($+\roundtwo  {1.65704}\text  { pN}$) to the seven-track 1D radial $N=3$ Cantor baseline (\texttt  {F0\_000}, $+\roundtwo  {3.17743}\text  { pN}$), single-mask 2D $(r,\theta )$ Cantor ring (\texttt  {F2rt\_110}, $+\roundtwo  {13.544}\text  { pN}$), and unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt  {F3\_111}, $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$).}}{28}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rotational_clutch_architecture}{{1}{28}{\textbf {Zero-overlap PFA cancellation and unified 3D conformal-recursive polar Cantor $(r, \theta , z)$ rotational clutch architecture (\texttt {F3\_111}) in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Two-dimensional cross-sectional schematic comparing Euclidean parallel plates ($A_{\rm overlap} > 0$, dominated by attractive proximity-force scaling $F_z^{\rm PFA} \propto -A_{\rm overlap}/d^4$), uniform periodic slot-tooth interdigitation ($A_{\rm overlap} = 0$, limited by single-scale evanescent screening at $\kappa \sim \pi /W_0$), and unified 3D prefractal Cantor interdigitation ($U=(1,1,1)$ in $(r,\theta ,z)$, with radial sub-slots $W_k = W_1 b^{-(k-1)}$, azimuthal Cantor lobe sub-apertures, and stepped vertical depths $H_m \in \{90, 80, 70\}\text { nm}$ partitioning transverse fringing fields across separated wavenumber sub-bands). \textbf {b}, Three-dimensional cutaway render of the optimal unified 3D polar Cantor clutch (\texttt {F3\_111}, $C_4$ symmetry, $90^\circ $ sector period, $R \in [\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackRInUm {}, \FractalNthreeCantorseventrackROutUm {}]\ \mu \text {m}$) in the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $). In each $90^\circ $ sector, $12$ radial rotor sub-teeth split azimuthally into $24$ stepped 3D Cantor lobes ($96$ lobes total across all four sectors; colour-coded by prefractal generation in Sector~$0$ as gold $m=1$ [$H_1 = 90\text { nm}$], orange $m=2$ [$H_2 = 80\text { nm}$], and coral $m=3$ [$H_3 = 70\text { nm}$]) interdigitate inside $12$ Cantor stator sub-slots bounded by $8$ primary gold stator ribs and $5$ internal copper-gold Cantor stator sub-ribs ($25\text { nm}$ membrane thickness, $z \in [-25, 0]\text { nm}$) suspended above recessed azimuthal landing pads ($150\text { nm}$ thickness, top surface at $z_{\rm pad,top} = -115\text { nm}$) and supported by a twin-forked single-crystal $\text {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ spider suspension. \textbf {c},\textbf {d}, Cutaway renders and axial-radial $(r,z)$ cross-sections of \texttt {F3\_111} in (\textbf {c}) the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $, $A_{\rm overlap} = 0$, $F_z^{\rm PFA} = 0$, showing upward saddle-point repulsive force $F_z = +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$ and areal density $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFa }\text { pN}\,\mu \text {m}^{-2}$ across the stepped tips $z_{{\rm tip},m} \in \{-90, -80, -70\}\text { nm}$, remaining repulsive at $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedThetatwooneFzPn }\text { pN}$ at the $\theta = 21^\circ $ straddling transition) and (\textbf {d}) the engaged landing-pad state ($\theta = 48^\circ $, $A_{\rm overlap} = \roundthree {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedAreaUmtwo }\ \mu \text {m}^2$ across the stepped vertical gaps $d_m \in \{25, 35, 45\}\text { nm}$ above $z_{\rm pad,top} = -115\text { nm}$, switching to strong normal attraction $F_z = \roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedThetafoureightFzPn }\text { pN}$). \textbf {e}, Six-stage radial cross-sectional progression across $r \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text {m}$ from the single-track baseline ($N=0$, $+\roundtwo {\SingletoothTrackzeroBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$), three-track uniform grating ($+\roundtwo {\CtrlUniformperiodicBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$), and stepped $(r,z)$ $N=2$ Cantor ring ($+\roundtwo {\CantorNtwoHybridrzBemStdFZPn }\text { pN}$) to the seven-track 1D radial $N=3$ Cantor baseline (\texttt {F0\_000}, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFzerozerozeroFzPn }\text { pN}$), single-mask 2D $(r,\theta )$ Cantor ring (\texttt {F2rt\_110}, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneonezeroRthetaPlanarFzPn }\text { pN}$), and unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt {F3\_111}, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$)}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Multiscale Cantor force amplification and rotational switching across the six-step benchmark in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Single-tooth vertical interdigitation ($N=0$) across tooth tip elevation $z_{\rm  tip} \in [-115, -55]\text  { nm}$, showing open-slot repulsive force ($+\roundtwo  {0.7067}\text  { pN}$ at $z_{\rm  tip} = -100\text  { nm}$) and sign reversal to attraction ($\roundtwo  {-0.359635}\text  { pN}$) under symmetric overhang ($z_{\rm  tip} = -55\text  { nm}$). \textbf  {b}, Zero-bias rotational switching ($\theta = 0^\circ $ to $48^\circ $) of axial Casimir force $F_z(\theta )$ (left axis) and normalized landing-pad overlap fraction $A_{\rm  overlap}/A_{\rm  tooth}$ (right axis) across the $N=0$ baseline, tight-slot $N=2$, compact $N=2$, seven-track 1D $N=3$ Cantor, and unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor (\texttt  {F3\_111}, $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =3^\circ $, $+\roundtwo  {2.88865}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =21^\circ $, and $\roundtwo  {-19.9798}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =48^\circ $) clutches. \textbf  {c}, Progression across prefractal generations $N = 0 \to 3$ on the matched Standard BEM mesh, reaching $+\roundtwo  {3.17743}\text  { pN}$ open-slot repulsive force ($4.5{}\times $ over $N=0$) and $\roundtwo  {-14.0388}\text  { pN}$ engaged attraction in 1D radial $N=3$, and advancing to $+\roundtwo  {13.544}\text  { pN}$ in single-mask 2D $(r,\theta )$ Cantor (\texttt  {F2rt\_110}) and $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ open-slot repulsion / $\roundtwo  {-19.9798}\text  { pN}$ engaged attraction ($\roundone  {38.5306}\text  { pN}$ peak-to-peak swing) in unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor (\texttt  {F3\_111}). \textbf  {d}, Comparison of $N=2$ (3-track), 1D $N=3$ (7-track), and unified 3D $N=3$ (12-sub-slot / 24-lobe) Cantor hierarchies against matched non-fractal control families (single wide tooth, 3-track, 7-track, and 12-sub-slot uniform periodic gratings, size-matched monotonic arrays, and randomly permuted 7-track and 12-sub-slot controls). \textbf  {e}, Active-tooth-area normalized repulsive force density $F_z/A_{\rm  tooth}$ across all evaluated $N=2$, 1D $N=3$, and unified 3D $N=3$ hierarchies and controls, peaking at $\roundtwo  {60.8337}\text  { pN}\,\mu \text  {m}^{-2}$ in \texttt  {F3\_111} ($\roundtwo  {44.4147}\text  { pN}\,\mu \text  {m}^{-2}$ in \texttt  {F2rt\_110}). \textbf  {f}, Active-only versus full-monolithic NEMS structural assemblies incorporating spider spokes, hub collars, and substrate trenches ($<3.3\%$ support crosstalk).}}{29}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:quantum_clutch_architecture_and_narrative}{{2}{29}{\textbf {Multiscale Cantor force amplification and rotational switching across the six-step benchmark in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Single-tooth vertical interdigitation ($N=0$) across tooth tip elevation $z_{\rm tip} \in [-115, -55]\text { nm}$, showing open-slot repulsive force ($+\roundtwo {\SingletoothTrackzeroBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$ at $z_{\rm tip} = -100\text { nm}$) and sign reversal to attraction ($\roundtwo {\SingletoothTrackzeroOverhangBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$) under symmetric overhang ($z_{\rm tip} = -55\text { nm}$). \textbf {b}, Zero-bias rotational switching ($\theta = 0^\circ $ to $48^\circ $) of axial Casimir force $F_z(\theta )$ (left axis) and normalized landing-pad overlap fraction $A_{\rm overlap}/A_{\rm tooth}$ (right axis) across the $N=0$ baseline, tight-slot $N=2$, compact $N=2$, seven-track 1D $N=3$ Cantor, and unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor (\texttt {F3\_111}, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =3^\circ $, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedThetatwooneFzPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =21^\circ $, and $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedThetafoureightFzPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =48^\circ $) clutches. \textbf {c}, Progression across prefractal generations $N = 0 \to 3$ on the matched Standard BEM mesh, reaching $+\roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$ open-slot repulsive force ($\FractalNthreeVsNzeroBemStdRatio {}\times $ over $N=0$) and $\roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetafoureightFZPn }\text { pN}$ engaged attraction in 1D radial $N=3$, and advancing to $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneonezeroRthetaPlanarFzPn }\text { pN}$ in single-mask 2D $(r,\theta )$ Cantor (\texttt {F2rt\_110}) and $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$ open-slot repulsion / $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedThetafoureightFzPn }\text { pN}$ engaged attraction ($\roundone {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedSwingPn }\text { pN}$ peak-to-peak swing) in unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor (\texttt {F3\_111}). \textbf {d}, Comparison of $N=2$ (3-track), 1D $N=3$ (7-track), and unified 3D $N=3$ (12-sub-slot / 24-lobe) Cantor hierarchies against matched non-fractal control families (single wide tooth, 3-track, 7-track, and 12-sub-slot uniform periodic gratings, size-matched monotonic arrays, and randomly permuted 7-track and 12-sub-slot controls). \textbf {e}, Active-tooth-area normalized repulsive force density $F_z/A_{\rm tooth}$ across all evaluated $N=2$, 1D $N=3$, and unified 3D $N=3$ hierarchies and controls, peaking at $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFa }\text { pN}\,\mu \text {m}^{-2}$ in \texttt {F3\_111} ($\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneonezeroRthetaPlanarFa }\text { pN}\,\mu \text {m}^{-2}$ in \texttt {F2rt\_110}). \textbf {f}, Active-only versus full-monolithic NEMS structural assemblies incorporating spider spokes, hub collars, and substrate trenches ($<3.3\%$ support crosstalk)}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Discretization sensitivity, corner-rounding regularization, and cross-solver benchmarks in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Repulsive-state ($\theta = 3^\circ \text  {--}6^\circ $) surface-mesh refinement across Standard ($1504{}$ panels), High ($3120{}$ panels), and Ultra-High ($6016{}$ panels) discretizations for $N=2$ ($3168{}$ and $6576{}$ panels for 1D $N=3$, and $6{,}784$ four-sector panels for unified 3D \texttt  {F3\_111} at $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ and planar 2D \texttt  {F2rt\_110} at $+\roundtwo  {13.544}\text  { pN}$) comparing sharp-edge ($r_{\rm  edge} = 0$) and lithographically rounded ($r_{\rm  edge} = 5\text  { nm}$) 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM and diagnostic 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM (top), alongside the Cantor-to-uniform repulsive gain ratio $F_z^{\rm  Cantor}/F_z^{\rm  unif}$ across mesh tiers including unified 3D \texttt  {F3\_111} ($1.33\times $ over 12-tooth uniform \texttt  {C6\_Uni12} and $\roundtwo  {9.02581}\times $ over 7-track uniform \texttt  {C1\_Uni000}, bottom). \textbf  {b}, Attractive-state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text  {--}48^\circ $) boundary-element continuum extrapolations ($h = N_{\rm  panels}^{-1/2} \to 0$) compared against 4-pass inclusion--exclusion 3D FDTD MEEP benchmarks and Scalar-Yukawa High-mesh bounds. \textbf  {c}, Cross-solver sign and magnitude comparison (on a symmetric logarithmic scale) across 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM, 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM, 4-pass 3D FDTD ($R=50$), and 1D Lifshitz--PFA across 14 disengaged repulsive, straddling transition, and engaged attractive states spanning $N=0$, $N=2$, 1D $N=3$, and unified 3D \texttt  {F3\_111} ($\theta =3^\circ , 21^\circ , 48^\circ $). \textbf  {d}, Imaginary-frequency Gauss--Legendre quadrature convergence across $n_\xi \in \{16, 24, 32, 40, 64\}$ ($\roundfour  {0.00242971}\%$ drift for $n_\xi \ge 24$, top) and fixed-standoff ($\delta _{\rm  box} = 10{}\text  { nm}$) 4-pass FDTD resolution scaling across $R \in \{40, 50, 60, 80\}$ ($\roundtwo  {3.1519}\%$ drift between $R=60$ and $R=80$, bottom).}}{30}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:quantum_clutch_3solver_verification}{{3}{30}{\textbf {Discretization sensitivity, corner-rounding regularization, and cross-solver benchmarks in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Repulsive-state ($\theta = 3^\circ \text {--}6^\circ $) surface-mesh refinement across Standard ($\RotCfourTightslotNtwoStandardThetaZerozerosixpzeroPanelCount {}$ panels), High ($\RotCfourTightslotNtwoHighThetaZerozerosixpzeroPanelCount {}$ panels), and Ultra-High ($\RotCfourTightslotNtwoUltraHighThetaZerozerosixpzeroPanelCount {}$ panels) discretizations for $N=2$ ($\RotConezeroFractalNthreeStandardThetaZerozerothreepzeroPanelCount {}$ and $\RotConezeroFractalNthreeHighThetaZerozerothreepzeroPanelCount {}$ panels for 1D $N=3$, and $6{,}784$ four-sector panels for unified 3D \texttt {F3\_111} at $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$ and planar 2D \texttt {F2rt\_110} at $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneonezeroRthetaPlanarFzPn }\text { pN}$) comparing sharp-edge ($r_{\rm edge} = 0$) and lithographically rounded ($r_{\rm edge} = 5\text { nm}$) 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM and diagnostic 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM (top), alongside the Cantor-to-uniform repulsive gain ratio $F_z^{\rm Cantor}/F_z^{\rm unif}$ across mesh tiers including unified 3D \texttt {F3\_111} ($1.33\times $ over 12-tooth uniform \texttt {C6\_Uni12} and $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedRatioFoneoneoneVsUnizerozerozero }\times $ over 7-track uniform \texttt {C1\_Uni000}, bottom). \textbf {b}, Attractive-state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text {--}48^\circ $) boundary-element continuum extrapolations ($h = N_{\rm panels}^{-1/2} \to 0$) compared against 4-pass inclusion--exclusion 3D FDTD MEEP benchmarks and Scalar-Yukawa High-mesh bounds. \textbf {c}, Cross-solver sign and magnitude comparison (on a symmetric logarithmic scale) across 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM, 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM, 4-pass 3D FDTD ($R=50$), and 1D Lifshitz--PFA across 14 disengaged repulsive, straddling transition, and engaged attractive states spanning $N=0$, $N=2$, 1D $N=3$, and unified 3D \texttt {F3\_111} ($\theta =3^\circ , 21^\circ , 48^\circ $). \textbf {d}, Imaginary-frequency Gauss--Legendre quadrature convergence across $n_\xi \in \{16, 24, 32, 40, 64\}$ ($\roundfour {\BemConvNxiDriftPct }\%$ drift for $n_\xi \ge 24$, top) and fixed-standoff ($\delta _{\rm box} = \MeepFixedboxMarginNm {}\text { nm}$) 4-pass FDTD resolution scaling across $R \in \{40, 50, 60, 80\}$ ($\roundtwo {\MeepFixedboxRsixzeroToReightzeroDriftPct }\%$ drift between $R=60$ and $R=80$, bottom)}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Spectral wavenumber partitioning and multi-stage vertical stroke response in the 3D Cantor clutch in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Normalized 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM diagnostic radial-wall coupling norm $w_m(\kappa )/\max $ and exact signed Casimir force integrand decomposition $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{m=1}^{3}\kappa f_{z,m}(\kappa )/\max $ across logarithmic imaginary wavenumber $\ln (\kappa \cdot 1\ \mu \text  {m})$ for the coplanar third-generation seven-track Cantor ring ($N=3$, $b=3$, radial clearances $g_{r,1}=135\text  { nm}$, $g_{r,2}=45\text  { nm}$, $g_{r,3}=15\text  { nm}$; peak $+\roundtwo  {0.37448}\text  { pN}$, trace decomposition residual $<10^{-16}\text  { pN}\cdot \mu \text  {m}$; spectral peaks at $\ln \kappa = \roundtwo  {2.70677}, \roundtwo  {3.3415}, \text  {and } \roundtwo  {3.8446}$) and the unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt  {F3\_111}, peak $+7.14\text  { pN}$ at $\ln \kappa = 1.92$ [$\kappa = 6.79\ \mu \text  {m}^{-1}$], a $19.1\times $ spectral integrand peak gain) compared against the three-track uniform periodic control. Dashed vertical lines mark the inverse radial clearance scales $\kappa = 1/g_{r,m}$. \textbf  {b}, Scale-compensated repulsive force $|z_{\rm  rotor}|^2 F_z(z_{\rm  rotor})$ swept across $36$ logarithmically spaced vertical stroke depths $|z_{\rm  rotor}| \in [25, 450]\text  { nm}$ ($\ln (|z_{\rm  rotor}|/\ell _3) \in [-0.47, 2.42]$) in a three-generation $(r,z)$-stepped Cantor clutch ($b=2.5{}$, geometrically spaced stator stage elevations $|z_{{\rm  stage},m}| \in \{250, 100, 40\}\text  { nm}$) versus a non-geometric three-stage control with linearly spaced elevations ($|z_{\rm  stage}| \in \{250, 145, 40\}\text  { nm}$) and a single-scale three-track uniform control ($|z_{\rm  stage}| = 100\text  { nm}$). Dotted vertical lines indicate the designed logarithmic stage intervals $\Delta \ln |z| = \ln b = \roundthree  {0.916291}$. \textbf  {c}, Detrended modulation $\delta (|z|^2 F_z)$ and $95\%$ regression confidence band from a simultaneous joint quadratic-plus-harmonic least-squares fit to Eq.~\eqref  {eq:fourier_running} at the geometric scaling frequency $\omega _1 = 2\pi /\ln b = \roundtwo  {6.8572}$ ($R^2 = \roundtwo  {0.529}$, $F = \roundtwo  {7.9214}$, $p = 1.9 \times 10^{-4}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {AIC} = \roundone  {-18.5828}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {BIC} = \roundone  {-12.2487}$ for the stepped Cantor clutch, versus $R^2 = \roundtwo  {0.176312}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {AIC} = +\roundone  {1.35448}$ for the linear three-stage control and $R^2 = \roundtwo  {0.0141241}$ for the single-scale uniform control). Inset: unconstrained free-frequency Lomb--Scargle variance-explained spectrum $R^2(\omega )$ swept across $\omega \in [1.0, 14.0]$, recovering $\hat  {\omega }_1 = \roundtwo  {6.45848} \pm \roundtwo  {0.345342}$ and scale factor $\hat  {b} = \exp (2\pi /\hat  {\omega }_1) = \roundtwo  {2.6455} \pm \roundtwo  {0.138461}$ ($95\%\text  { CI}$, peak $R^2(\hat  {\omega }_1) = \roundtwo  {0.586987}$).}}{31}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:clutch_log_periodicity}{{4}{31}{\textbf {Spectral wavenumber partitioning and multi-stage vertical stroke response in the 3D Cantor clutch in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Normalized 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM diagnostic radial-wall coupling norm $w_m(\kappa )/\max $ and exact signed Casimir force integrand decomposition $\sum _{m=1}^{3}\kappa f_{z,m}(\kappa )/\max $ across logarithmic imaginary wavenumber $\ln (\kappa \cdot 1\ \mu \text {m})$ for the coplanar third-generation seven-track Cantor ring ($N=3$, $b=3$, radial clearances $g_{r,1}=135\text { nm}$, $g_{r,2}=45\text { nm}$, $g_{r,3}=15\text { nm}$; peak $+\roundtwo {\LogperSignedKfTotalPeakPn }\text { pN}$, trace decomposition residual $<10^{-16}\text { pN}\cdot \mu \text {m}$; spectral peaks at $\ln \kappa = \roundtwo {\LogperLnKPeakLone }, \roundtwo {\LogperLnKPeakLtwo }, \text {and } \roundtwo {\LogperLnKPeakLthree }$) and the unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt {F3\_111}, peak $+7.14\text { pN}$ at $\ln \kappa = 1.92$ [$\kappa = 6.79\ \mu \text {m}^{-1}$], a $19.1\times $ spectral integrand peak gain) compared against the three-track uniform periodic control. Dashed vertical lines mark the inverse radial clearance scales $\kappa = 1/g_{r,m}$. \textbf {b}, Scale-compensated repulsive force $|z_{\rm rotor}|^2 F_z(z_{\rm rotor})$ swept across $36$ logarithmically spaced vertical stroke depths $|z_{\rm rotor}| \in [25, 450]\text { nm}$ ($\ln (|z_{\rm rotor}|/\ell _3) \in [-0.47, 2.42]$) in a three-generation $(r,z)$-stepped Cantor clutch ($b=\LogperSteppedRzBScale {}$, geometrically spaced stator stage elevations $|z_{{\rm stage},m}| \in \{250, 100, 40\}\text { nm}$) versus a non-geometric three-stage control with linearly spaced elevations ($|z_{\rm stage}| \in \{250, 145, 40\}\text { nm}$) and a single-scale three-track uniform control ($|z_{\rm stage}| = 100\text { nm}$). Dotted vertical lines indicate the designed logarithmic stage intervals $\Delta \ln |z| = \ln b = \roundthree {\LogperSteppedRzLnB }$. \textbf {c}, Detrended modulation $\delta (|z|^2 F_z)$ and $95\%$ regression confidence band from a simultaneous joint quadratic-plus-harmonic least-squares fit to Eq.~\eqref {eq:fourier_running} at the geometric scaling frequency $\omega _1 = 2\pi /\ln b = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzOmegaone }$ ($R^2 = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzRtwo }$, $F = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzFstatCantor }$, $p = 1.9 \times 10^{-4}$, $\Delta \mathrm {AIC} = \roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaAicCantor }$, $\Delta \mathrm {BIC} = \roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaBicCantor }$ for the stepped Cantor clutch, versus $R^2 = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzRtwoLinear }$, $\Delta \mathrm {AIC} = +\roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaAicLinear }$ for the linear three-stage control and $R^2 = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzRtwoUniform }$ for the single-scale uniform control). Inset: unconstrained free-frequency Lomb--Scargle variance-explained spectrum $R^2(\omega )$ swept across $\omega \in [1.0, 14.0]$, recovering $\hat {\omega }_1 = \roundtwo {\LogperFreeOmegaoneCantor } \pm \roundtwo {\LogperFreeOmegaoneCininefiveHalfCantor }$ and scale factor $\hat {b} = \exp (2\pi /\hat {\omega }_1) = \roundtwo {\LogperFreeBHatCantor } \pm \roundtwo {\LogperFreeBHatCininefiveHalfCantor }$ ($95\%\text { CI}$, peak $R^2(\hat {\omega }_1) = \roundtwo {\LogperFreeRtwoPeakCantor }$)}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Unified 3D conformal-recursive polar Cantor $(r, \theta , z)$ $2^3$ factorial ablation, matched 7-tooth and 12-tooth control benchmarks, and 1D-to-3D log-periodic sub-band harvest in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Disengaged open-slot repulsive axial force $F_z(3^\circ )$ across all 19 evaluated $N=3$ architectures spanning $R \in [0.3{}, 1.65{}]\ \mu \text  {m}$ at invariant landing-pad elevation $z_{\rm  pad,top} = -115\text  { nm}$ and matched active tooth area ($A_{\rm  tooth} = \roundfour  {0.310389}\ \mu \text  {m}^2$, or $\roundfour  {0.304944}\ \mu \text  {m}^2$ when capped by the $28^\circ $ azimuthal envelope): the $2^3$ factorial hierarchy (F0-000 through F3-111, plus rotor-sub-teeth-only F1r-Sub), matched 7-tooth controls (C1-Uni000--C5-OutPhase), and matched 12-sub-slot / 12-tooth / 24-lobe controls (C6-Uni12--C10-OutPhase12). Horizontal dashed and dash-dotted lines mark the strongest 7-tooth control (C3-MonoGen, $+\roundtwo  {7.84204}\text  { pN}$) and strongest 12-tooth control (C9-Shuf12, $+\roundtwo  {15.1719}\text  { pN}$). \textbf  {b}, Per-slot axial force breakdown $F_{z,k}$ ($k=1,\dots  ,7$) across the seven primary radial stator bands, showing how internal stator Cantor sub-ribs (F1r-100) and full 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ recursion (F3-111) unlock the central $450\text  { nm}$ Generation-1 slot (S4) from $\roundfour  {-0.00343385}\text  { pN}$ in F0-000 to $+\roundtwo  {2.9393}\text  { pN}$ and $+\roundtwo  {5.42398}\text  { pN}$. \textbf  {c}, Total imaginary-wavenumber integrand $\kappa f_z(\kappa )$ across $\kappa \in [0.5, 40]\ \mu \text  {m}^{-1}$ comparing the factorial Cantor progression against 7-tooth and 12-tooth controls. \textbf  {d}, Progression from the 1D Eq.~\eqref  {eq:fourier_running} log-periodic oscillation $\cos (\omega _1\ln \kappa )$ ($\Delta \ln \kappa = \ln 3$, top dash-dotted wave) to 3D generation-resolved spectral integrands $\kappa f_{z,m}(\kappa )$ ($m=1,2,3$), showing how in-phase 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ recursion in \texttt  {F3\_111} activates the dormant Generation-1 ($\roundfour  {-0.00343385} \to +\roundtwo  {5.42398}\text  { pN}$) and weak Generation-2 ($+\roundtwo  {0.45854} \to +\roundtwo  {6.16879}\text  { pN}$) bands alongside Generation-3 ($+\roundtwo  {2.72233} \to +\roundtwo  {6.95809}\text  { pN}$) across $\kappa _1 = 2.41\ \mu \text  {m}^{-1}$, $\kappa _2 = 4.92\ \mu \text  {m}^{-1}$, and $\kappa _3 = 9.01\ \mu \text  {m}^{-1}$. Inset: step-by-step $1\text  {D} \to 3\text  {D}$ generation sub-band harvest ($+\roundtwo  {3.17743} \to +\roundtwo  {9.09096} \to +\roundtwo  {13.544} \to +\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$, a $\roundtwo  {5.83832}\times $ gain, versus $+\roundtwo  {14.2916}\text  { pN}$ when $(\theta ,z)$ phase locking is broken in \texttt  {C10\_OutPhase12}).}}{32}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:n3_unified_3d_fractal_factorial}{{5}{32}{\textbf {Unified 3D conformal-recursive polar Cantor $(r, \theta , z)$ $2^3$ factorial ablation, matched 7-tooth and 12-tooth control benchmarks, and 1D-to-3D log-periodic sub-band harvest in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Disengaged open-slot repulsive axial force $F_z(3^\circ )$ across all 19 evaluated $N=3$ architectures spanning $R \in [\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackRInUm {}, \FractalNthreeCantorseventrackROutUm {}]\ \mu \text {m}$ at invariant landing-pad elevation $z_{\rm pad,top} = -115\text { nm}$ and matched active tooth area ($A_{\rm tooth} = \roundfour {\NthreeUnithreedFzerozerozeroAreaUmtwo }\ \mu \text {m}^2$, or $\roundfour {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedAreaUmtwo }\ \mu \text {m}^2$ when capped by the $28^\circ $ azimuthal envelope): the $2^3$ factorial hierarchy (F0-000 through F3-111, plus rotor-sub-teeth-only F1r-Sub), matched 7-tooth controls (C1-Uni000--C5-OutPhase), and matched 12-sub-slot / 12-tooth / 24-lobe controls (C6-Uni12--C10-OutPhase12). Horizontal dashed and dash-dotted lines mark the strongest 7-tooth control (C3-MonoGen, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedCtrlMonogenFzPn }\text { pN}$) and strongest 12-tooth control (C9-Shuf12, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedCtrlShufonetwoFzPn }\text { pN}$). \textbf {b}, Per-slot axial force breakdown $F_{z,k}$ ($k=1,\dots ,7$) across the seven primary radial stator bands, showing how internal stator Cantor sub-ribs (F1r-100) and full 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ recursion (F3-111) unlock the central $450\text { nm}$ Generation-1 slot (S4) from $\roundfour {\NthreeUnithreedSlotfourFzerozerozeroPn }\text { pN}$ in F0-000 to $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedSlotfourFonezerozeroPn }\text { pN}$ and $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedSlotfourFoneoneonePn }\text { pN}$. \textbf {c}, Total imaginary-wavenumber integrand $\kappa f_z(\kappa )$ across $\kappa \in [0.5, 40]\ \mu \text {m}^{-1}$ comparing the factorial Cantor progression against 7-tooth and 12-tooth controls. \textbf {d}, Progression from the 1D Eq.~\eqref {eq:fourier_running} log-periodic oscillation $\cos (\omega _1\ln \kappa )$ ($\Delta \ln \kappa = \ln 3$, top dash-dotted wave) to 3D generation-resolved spectral integrands $\kappa f_{z,m}(\kappa )$ ($m=1,2,3$), showing how in-phase 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ recursion in \texttt {F3\_111} activates the dormant Generation-1 ($\roundfour {\NthreeUnithreedSlotfourFzerozerozeroPn } \to +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedSlotfourFoneoneonePn }\text { pN}$) and weak Generation-2 ($+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedGentwoFzerozerozeroPn } \to +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedGentwoFoneoneonePn }\text { pN}$) bands alongside Generation-3 ($+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedGenthreeFzerozerozeroPn } \to +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedGenthreeFoneoneonePn }\text { pN}$) across $\kappa _1 = 2.41\ \mu \text {m}^{-1}$, $\kappa _2 = 4.92\ \mu \text {m}^{-1}$, and $\kappa _3 = 9.01\ \mu \text {m}^{-1}$. Inset: step-by-step $1\text {D} \to 3\text {D}$ generation sub-band harvest ($+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFzerozerozeroFzPn } \to +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFonezerozeroRFzPn } \to +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneonezeroRthetaPlanarFzPn } \to +\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$, a $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedRatioFoneoneoneVsFzerozerozero }\times $ gain, versus $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedCtrlOutphaseonetwoFzPn }\text { pN}$ when $(\theta ,z)$ phase locking is broken in \texttt {C10\_OutPhase12})}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Room-temperature ($T=300{}\text  { K}$) thermal dispersion, electrostatic bias thresholds, flexure scaling, fabrication tolerances, rotational energy/torque, and thermomechanical lock-in SNR in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Thermal Matsubara dispersion across ideal PEC ($0\text  { K}$), Drude gold ($0\text  { K}$), and room-temperature Drude gold ($300\text  { K}$) for the stepped $(r,z)$ $N=2$ Cantor ring and compact $N=2$ variant alongside the unified 3D Cantor hierarchy (\texttt  {F3\_111}: $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =3^\circ $ and $\roundtwo  {-19.9798}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =48^\circ $). \textbf  {b}, Net repulsive restoring force $F_{z,\rm  net}$ across residual root-mean-square electrostatic bias voltages $V_{\rm  rms} \in [0, 100]\text  { mV}$, showing the critical uniform-bias thresholds ($V_{\rm  crit} = \roundone  {90.2392}\text  { mV}$ for $N=2$, $\roundone  {94.1128}\text  { mV}$ for Compact $N=2$, and $\roundone  {99.9121}\text  { mV}$ for 3D Cantor \texttt  {F3\_111} where $|\partial C_{\rm  el}/\partial z| = \roundfour  {0.0037167}\text  { pN}\,\text  {mV}^{-2}$) and the $<5\text  { mV}$ Kelvin-probe nulled mean-potential regime. \textbf  {c}, Destabilizing radial Earnshaw Casimir stiffness $|k_{r,\rm  Casimir}|$ ($\roundtwo  {-0.312377}\text  {--}\roundtwo  {-0.342416}\text  { pN}\,\text  {nm}^{-1}$ for $N=2$ and $\roundtwo  {3.49699}\text  { pN}\,\text  {nm}^{-1}$ for \texttt  {F3\_111}) compared on a logarithmic scale against the stabilizing four-spoke single-crystal $\text  {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ radial flexure stiffness $k_{r,\rm  mech}$ ($E_Y = \scinum  {1.69e+11}\text  { Pa}$) across isometric transducer (Regime~I: $\roundzero  {294.689}\times \text  {--}\roundzero  {3298.97}\times $ radial safety factor, $12\text  {--}\roundzero  {153.137}\text  { pm}$ lift), nanometre-stroke (Regime~II), and contact-release clutch (Regime~III) suspensions. \textbf  {d}, Room-temperature open-slot repulsive force $F_z(3^\circ )$ and rotational switching swing $\Delta F_z$ across critical-dimension tooth-width etch biases $\Delta w_{\rm  tooth} \in [-10, +10]\text  { nm}$ and EBL corner rounding $r_{\rm  edge} = 5\text  {--}10\text  { nm}$ (with \texttt  {F3\_111} nominal $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ and $\Delta F_z = \roundone  {38.5306}\text  { pN}$). \textbf  {e}, 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM rotational Casimir interaction energy landscape $\Delta E_C(\theta ) = E_C(\theta ) - E_C(0^\circ )$ (left axis) and axial-switching Casimir torque $\tau _\theta (\theta ) = -\partial E_C(\theta )/\partial \theta $ (right axis) across $\theta \in [0^\circ , 48^\circ ]$, highlighting the $\theta =18{}^\circ \text  {--}21^\circ $ sidewall-crossing potential well, state-to-state switching work $W_{\rm  switch}(48^\circ \!\to \!3^\circ ) = \roundtwo  {0.225905}\text  { eV}$, and peak torque $|\tau _\theta |_{\max } = \roundzero  {222.159}\text  {--}\roundzero  {386.708}\text  { pN}\cdot \text  {nm}$ across $N=2$ and $N=3$. \textbf  {f}, Room-temperature ($300\text  { K}$) thermomechanical lock-in force signal-to-noise ratio $\mathrm  {SNR}(\tau ) = F_{z,300\rm  K}^{\rm  rep}/\delta F_{\rm  th}(\tau )$ versus integration time $\tau \in [10^{-3}, 10^2]\text  { s}$ across Regimes~I--III for ultra-high-vacuum quality factors $Q = 10^4$ (solid) and $Q = 10^5$ (dashed), reaching $\mathrm  {SNR}(1\text  { s}) = \roundzero  {7231.95}\text  {--}\roundzero  {7345.33}$ for $N=2$ and $\roundzero  {77431.6}$ ($\roundzero  {2.45e+05}$ at $Q=10^5$) for 3D Cantor \texttt  {F3\_111} in Regime~I ($\delta z_{\rm  th} = \roundtwo  {0.18491}\text  { nm}$, $|\partial F_z/\partial z_0| = \roundtwo  {1.15943}\text  { pN}\,\text  {nm}^{-1}$).}}{33}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:nature_feasibility_stability}{{6}{33}{\textbf {Room-temperature ($T=\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoCdToleranceTemperatureK {}\text { K}$) thermal dispersion, electrostatic bias thresholds, flexure scaling, fabrication tolerances, rotational energy/torque, and thermomechanical lock-in SNR in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Thermal Matsubara dispersion across ideal PEC ($0\text { K}$), Drude gold ($0\text { K}$), and room-temperature Drude gold ($300\text { K}$) for the stepped $(r,z)$ $N=2$ Cantor ring and compact $N=2$ variant alongside the unified 3D Cantor hierarchy (\texttt {F3\_111}: $+\roundtwo {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneFRepThreezerozerokPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =3^\circ $ and $\roundtwo {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneFEngagedThreezerozerokPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =48^\circ $). \textbf {b}, Net repulsive restoring force $F_{z,\rm net}$ across residual root-mean-square electrostatic bias voltages $V_{\rm rms} \in [0, 100]\text { mV}$, showing the critical uniform-bias thresholds ($V_{\rm crit} = \roundone {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzPatchPotentialVCritMv }\text { mV}$ for $N=2$, $\roundone {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoPatchPotentialVCritMv }\text { mV}$ for Compact $N=2$, and $\roundone {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneVCritMv }\text { mV}$ for 3D Cantor \texttt {F3\_111} where $|\partial C_{\rm el}/\partial z| = \roundfour {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneAbsDcDzPnPerMvtwo }\text { pN}\,\text {mV}^{-2}$) and the $<5\text { mV}$ Kelvin-probe nulled mean-potential regime. \textbf {c}, Destabilizing radial Earnshaw Casimir stiffness $|k_{r,\rm Casimir}|$ ($\roundtwo {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzLateralStabilityKRCasimirPnPerNm }\text {--}\roundtwo {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoLateralStabilityOriginEvenEnergyEstimatePnPerNm }\text { pN}\,\text {nm}^{-1}$ for $N=2$ and $\roundtwo {\fpeval {abs(\NatureFthreeOneoneoneKRCasimirPnPerNm )}}\text { pN}\,\text {nm}^{-1}$ for \texttt {F3\_111}) compared on a logarithmic scale against the stabilizing four-spoke single-crystal $\text {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ radial flexure stiffness $k_{r,\rm mech}$ ($E_Y = \scinum {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoLateralStabilityEYPa }\text { Pa}$) across isometric transducer (Regime~I: $\roundzero {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneRegoneLateralStabilitySafetyFactor }\times \text {--}\roundzero {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzLateralStabilityLateralStabilitySafetyFactor }\times $ radial safety factor, $12\text {--}\roundzero {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneRegoneEquilibriumAxialRepulsiveLiftPm }\text { pm}$ lift), nanometre-stroke (Regime~II), and contact-release clutch (Regime~III) suspensions. \textbf {d}, Room-temperature open-slot repulsive force $F_z(3^\circ )$ and rotational switching swing $\Delta F_z$ across critical-dimension tooth-width etch biases $\Delta w_{\rm tooth} \in [-10, +10]\text { nm}$ and EBL corner rounding $r_{\rm edge} = 5\text {--}10\text { nm}$ (with \texttt {F3\_111} nominal $+\roundtwo {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneFRepThreezerozerokPn }\text { pN}$ and $\Delta F_z = \roundone {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneDeltaFSwingPn }\text { pN}$). \textbf {e}, 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM rotational Casimir interaction energy landscape $\Delta E_C(\theta ) = E_C(\theta ) - E_C(0^\circ )$ (left axis) and axial-switching Casimir torque $\tau _\theta (\theta ) = -\partial E_C(\theta )/\partial \theta $ (right axis) across $\theta \in [0^\circ , 48^\circ ]$, highlighting the $\theta =\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzRotationalEnergyBarrierThetaEnergyMinDeg {}^\circ \text {--}21^\circ $ sidewall-crossing potential well, state-to-state switching work $W_{\rm switch}(48^\circ \!\to \!3^\circ ) = \roundtwo {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzRotationalEnergyBarrierSwitchingWorkEv }\text { eV}$, and peak torque $|\tau _\theta |_{\max } = \roundzero {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoPeakTorquePnNm }\text {--}\roundzero {\NatureFractalNthreeCantorseventrackPeakTorquePnNm }\text { pN}\cdot \text {nm}$ across $N=2$ and $N=3$. \textbf {f}, Room-temperature ($300\text { K}$) thermomechanical lock-in force signal-to-noise ratio $\mathrm {SNR}(\tau ) = F_{z,300\rm K}^{\rm rep}/\delta F_{\rm th}(\tau )$ versus integration time $\tau \in [10^{-3}, 10^2]\text { s}$ across Regimes~I--III for ultra-high-vacuum quality factors $Q = 10^4$ (solid) and $Q = 10^5$ (dashed), reaching $\mathrm {SNR}(1\text { s}) = \roundzero {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoSnrOneSec }\text {--}\roundzero {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzSnrOneSec }$ for $N=2$ and $\roundzero {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneSnrOneSecQoneefour }$ ($\roundzero {\NatureFthreeOneoneoneSnrOneSecQoneefive }$ at $Q=10^5$) for 3D Cantor \texttt {F3\_111} in Regime~I ($\delta z_{\rm th} = \roundtwo {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzThermomechanicalNoiseThermalDzRegimeOneNm }\text { nm}$, $|\partial F_z/\partial z_0| = \roundtwo {\fpeval {abs(\NatureFthreeOneoneoneDfzDzzeroPnPerNm )}}\text { pN}\,\text {nm}^{-1}$)}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Three-dimensional geometric atlas across all 15 evaluated radial and unified 3D cavity constellations in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} Individual 3D cutaway portraits and radial cross-section $(r, z)$ geometry bars across the 12 radial constellations (\textbf  {a}--\textbf  {l}) and 3 representative unified 3D polar Cantor configurations (\textbf  {m}--\textbf  {o}): \textbf  {a}, $N=0$ symmetric overhang (SingleTooth-Track0, $z_{\rm  tip} = -55\text  { nm}$); \textbf  {b}, $N=0$ deep interdigitation (SingleTooth-Track0, $z_{\rm  tip} = -100\text  { nm}$); \textbf  {c}, $N=1$ fundamental Cantor slot (Fractal-N1-FundRing); \textbf  {d}, single wide tooth control (Ctrl-SingleWide); \textbf  {e}, uniform periodic grating control (Ctrl-UniformPeriodic); \textbf  {f}, size-matched monotonic array control (Ctrl-SizeMatched-Monotonic); \textbf  {g}, uniform-depth $N=2$ Cantor ring (Cantor-N2-FlatZ, $H_1 = H_2 = 100\text  { nm}$); \textbf  {h}, $(r,z)$-scaled $N=2$ Cantor ring (Cantor-N2-HybridRZ, $H_1 = 100\text  { nm}$, $H_2 = 90\text  { nm}$); \textbf  {i}, compact $N=2$ rotational variant (Compact-N2); \textbf  {j}, tight-slot $N=2$ rotational variant (TightSlot-N2); \textbf  {k}, third-generation seven-track Cantor ring ($N=3$, Cantor-N3-7Track, $28$ teeth); \textbf  {l}, full-monolithic $N=2$ and $N=3$ structural assemblies incorporating four radial spider spokes, hub collars, and lower substrate isolation trenches; \textbf  {m}, unified 1D radial Cantor hierarchy (\texttt  {F1r\_100}, $12$ rotor sub-teeth and $5$ copper-gold Cantor stator sub-ribs per sector, $+\roundtwo  {9.09096}\text  { pN}$); \textbf  {n}, single-mask planar 2D $(r,\theta )$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt  {F2rt\_110}, $12$ sub-teeth split into $24$ azimuthal lobes per sector, $+\roundtwo  {13.544}\text  { pN}$); and \textbf  {o}, unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt  {F3\_111}, $12$ sub-teeth, $24$ lobes, and $3$ axial $z$-tiers per sector, $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =3^\circ $ and $\roundtwo  {-19.9798}\text  { pN}$ at $\theta =48^\circ $).}}{34}{figure.ext.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:all_constellations_blender}{{1}{34}{\textbf {Three-dimensional geometric atlas across all 15 evaluated radial and unified 3D cavity constellations in vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} Individual 3D cutaway portraits and radial cross-section $(r, z)$ geometry bars across the 12 radial constellations (\textbf {a}--\textbf {l}) and 3 representative unified 3D polar Cantor configurations (\textbf {m}--\textbf {o}): \textbf {a}, $N=0$ symmetric overhang (SingleTooth-Track0, $z_{\rm tip} = -55\text { nm}$); \textbf {b}, $N=0$ deep interdigitation (SingleTooth-Track0, $z_{\rm tip} = -100\text { nm}$); \textbf {c}, $N=1$ fundamental Cantor slot (Fractal-N1-FundRing); \textbf {d}, single wide tooth control (Ctrl-SingleWide); \textbf {e}, uniform periodic grating control (Ctrl-UniformPeriodic); \textbf {f}, size-matched monotonic array control (Ctrl-SizeMatched-Monotonic); \textbf {g}, uniform-depth $N=2$ Cantor ring (Cantor-N2-FlatZ, $H_1 = H_2 = 100\text { nm}$); \textbf {h}, $(r,z)$-scaled $N=2$ Cantor ring (Cantor-N2-HybridRZ, $H_1 = 100\text { nm}$, $H_2 = 90\text { nm}$); \textbf {i}, compact $N=2$ rotational variant (Compact-N2); \textbf {j}, tight-slot $N=2$ rotational variant (TightSlot-N2); \textbf {k}, third-generation seven-track Cantor ring ($N=3$, Cantor-N3-7Track, $28$ teeth); \textbf {l}, full-monolithic $N=2$ and $N=3$ structural assemblies incorporating four radial spider spokes, hub collars, and lower substrate isolation trenches; \textbf {m}, unified 1D radial Cantor hierarchy (\texttt {F1r\_100}, $12$ rotor sub-teeth and $5$ copper-gold Cantor stator sub-ribs per sector, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFonezerozeroRFzPn }\text { pN}$); \textbf {n}, single-mask planar 2D $(r,\theta )$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt {F2rt\_110}, $12$ sub-teeth split into $24$ azimuthal lobes per sector, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneonezeroRthetaPlanarFzPn }\text { pN}$); and \textbf {o}, unified 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ Cantor hierarchy (\texttt {F3\_111}, $12$ sub-teeth, $24$ lobes, and $3$ axial $z$-tiers per sector, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =3^\circ $ and $\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedThetafoureightFzPn }\text { pN}$ at $\theta =48^\circ $)}{figure.ext.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Seven-track radial ordering, cylindrical curvature decoupling, and 3D fractal reversal in 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Open-slot repulsive force $F_z(3^\circ )$ across the seven-track uniform periodic (Ctrl-Uniform-7Track), randomly permuted (Ctrl-RandomPermuted-7Track), symmetric Cantor (Cantor-N3-7Track), and inner-packed monotonic (Ctrl-Monotonic-7Track) rings in the curved cylindrical annulus $R \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text  {m}$ ($R_{\max }/R_{\min } = 5.5$, blue) versus the arc-matched quasi-planar annulus $R \in [10.0, 11.35]\ \mu \text  {m}$ ($R_{\max }/R_{\min } = 1.135$, orange), showing the $\roundone  {14.2723}$-fold collapse of the 1D monotonic-over-Cantor gap from $+\roundone  {38.0169}\%$ to $+\roundtwo  {2.66369}\%$, followed by the 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ fractal reversal where 7-track PeakSync Cantor ($+\roundtwo  {4.87766}\text  { pN}$) beats 7-track PeakSync Monotonic ($+\roundtwo  {4.32897}\text  { pN}$) by $+\roundone  {12.6748}\%$ and 12-tooth unified 3D Cantor (\texttt  {F3\_111}, $+\roundtwo  {18.5509}\text  { pN}$) beats 12-tooth unified 3D Monotonic (\texttt  {C8\_Mono12}, $+\roundtwo  {15.0679}\text  { pN}$) by $+\roundone  {23.1148}\%$. \textbf  {b}, Per-track axial force $F_{z,k}(R_k)$ versus track centre radius $R_k$ across $50\text  { nm}$ ($g_{r,3}=15\text  { nm}$), $150\text  { nm}$ ($g_{r,2}=45\text  { nm}$), and $450\text  { nm}$ ($g_{r,1}=135\text  { nm}$) slots in cylindrical and quasi-planar coordinates. \textbf  {c}, Distribution of total repulsive force $F_z = \DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{k=1}^7 F_{z,k}$ across $N_{\rm  perm} = \roundzero  {30}$ directly evaluated non-Cantor multiset permutations plus the Cantor baseline ($31$ direct 3D BEM evaluations, dark blue) and the 105-permutation radial-polynomial surrogate (light blue). \textbf  {d}, Circumference-normalized repulsive density $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{k=1}^7 F_{z,k}/(2\pi R_k)$ versus mean radial centre $\bar  {R}_{50}$ of the four $50\text  { nm}$ slots, placing the symmetric Cantor sequence at the exact median ($\roundzero  {50}\text  {th}$ percentile, $+\roundthree  {0.818327}\text  { pN}\,\mu \text  {m}^{-1}$).}}{35}{figure.ext.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:n3_7track_ordering_curvature}{{2}{35}{\textbf {Seven-track radial ordering, cylindrical curvature decoupling, and 3D fractal reversal in 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Open-slot repulsive force $F_z(3^\circ )$ across the seven-track uniform periodic (Ctrl-Uniform-7Track), randomly permuted (Ctrl-RandomPermuted-7Track), symmetric Cantor (Cantor-N3-7Track), and inner-packed monotonic (Ctrl-Monotonic-7Track) rings in the curved cylindrical annulus $R \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text {m}$ ($R_{\max }/R_{\min } = 5.5$, blue) versus the arc-matched quasi-planar annulus $R \in [10.0, 11.35]\ \mu \text {m}$ ($R_{\max }/R_{\min } = 1.135$, orange), showing the $\roundone {\NthreeCurvGapReductionFactor }$-fold collapse of the 1D monotonic-over-Cantor gap from $+\roundone {\NthreeCurvCylMonoVsCantorPct }\%$ to $+\roundtwo {\NthreeCurvQparcMonoVsCantorPct }\%$, followed by the 3D $(r,\theta ,z)$ fractal reversal where 7-track PeakSync Cantor ($+\roundtwo {\NthreePeaksyncCantorIsoareaFzPn }\text { pN}$) beats 7-track PeakSync Monotonic ($+\roundtwo {\NthreePeaksyncCtrlMonoSameradFzPn }\text { pN}$) by $+\roundone {\NthreePeaksyncGainIsoVsMonoSameradPct }\%$ and 12-tooth unified 3D Cantor (\texttt {F3\_111}, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedFoneoneoneUnifiedFzPn }\text { pN}$) beats 12-tooth unified 3D Monotonic (\texttt {C8\_Mono12}, $+\roundtwo {\NthreeUnithreedCtrlMonoonetwoFzPn }\text { pN}$) by $+\roundone {\NthreeUnithreedGainFoneoneoneVsMonoonetwoPct }\%$. \textbf {b}, Per-track axial force $F_{z,k}(R_k)$ versus track centre radius $R_k$ across $50\text { nm}$ ($g_{r,3}=15\text { nm}$), $150\text { nm}$ ($g_{r,2}=45\text { nm}$), and $450\text { nm}$ ($g_{r,1}=135\text { nm}$) slots in cylindrical and quasi-planar coordinates. \textbf {c}, Distribution of total repulsive force $F_z = \sum _{k=1}^7 F_{z,k}$ across $N_{\rm perm} = \roundzero {\NthreePermNEvaluated }$ directly evaluated non-Cantor multiset permutations plus the Cantor baseline ($31$ direct 3D BEM evaluations, dark blue) and the 105-permutation radial-polynomial surrogate (light blue). \textbf {d}, Circumference-normalized repulsive density $\sum _{k=1}^7 F_{z,k}/(2\pi R_k)$ versus mean radial centre $\bar {R}_{50}$ of the four $50\text { nm}$ slots, placing the symmetric Cantor sequence at the exact median ($\roundzero {\NthreePermCantorPctFcircEval }\text {th}$ percentile, $+\roundthree {\NthreeCurvCylCantorFcircPnPerUm }\text { pN}\,\mu \text {m}^{-1}$)}{figure.ext.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Three-dimensional Blender structural and geometric audit atlas across all 19 unified 3D polar Cantor factorial and matched-control configurations ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} Perspective 3D renders across the $2^3$ factorial hierarchy (\textbf  {a}--\textbf  {i}, F0-000 through F3-111, including F1r-Sub), matched 7-tooth controls (\textbf  {j}--\textbf  {n}, C1-Uni000--C5-OutPhase), and matched 12-sub-slot / 12-tooth / 24-lobe controls (\textbf  {o}--\textbf  {s}, C6-Uni12--C10-OutPhase12) spanning $R \in [0.3{}, 1.65{}]\ \mu \text  {m}$ above the invariant recessed landing pad ($z_{\rm  pad,top} = -115\text  { nm}$). Bright copper highlights the internal solid stator Cantor sub-ribs ($u_r = 1$), while gold, amber, and crimson denote Generations 1, 2, and 3 rotor sub-teeth and azimuthal Cantor lobes. All $19{}/19{}$ configurations pass automated 3D mesh/clearance verification (Audit: PASS; active tooth area error $\le \roundfour  {0.000631698}\ \mu \text  {m}^2$, radial clearance $\ge 15{}\text  { nm}$, axial clearance $\ge 15{}\text  { nm}$).}}{36}{figure.ext.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:n3_unified_3d_blender_atlas}{{3}{36}{\textbf {Three-dimensional Blender structural and geometric audit atlas across all 19 unified 3D polar Cantor factorial and matched-control configurations ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} Perspective 3D renders across the $2^3$ factorial hierarchy (\textbf {a}--\textbf {i}, F0-000 through F3-111, including F1r-Sub), matched 7-tooth controls (\textbf {j}--\textbf {n}, C1-Uni000--C5-OutPhase), and matched 12-sub-slot / 12-tooth / 24-lobe controls (\textbf {o}--\textbf {s}, C6-Uni12--C10-OutPhase12) spanning $R \in [\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackRInUm {}, \FractalNthreeCantorseventrackROutUm {}]\ \mu \text {m}$ above the invariant recessed landing pad ($z_{\rm pad,top} = -115\text { nm}$). Bright copper highlights the internal solid stator Cantor sub-ribs ($u_r = 1$), while gold, amber, and crimson denote Generations 1, 2, and 3 rotor sub-teeth and azimuthal Cantor lobes. All $\NthreeBlenderAuditPassedConfigs {}/\NthreeBlenderAuditTotalConfigs {}$ configurations pass automated 3D mesh/clearance verification (Audit: PASS; active tooth area error $\le \roundfour {\NthreeBlenderAuditMaxAreaErrUmtwo }\ \mu \text {m}^2$, radial clearance $\ge \NthreeBlenderAuditMinRadialClearanceNm {}\text { nm}$, axial clearance $\ge \NthreeBlenderAuditMinAxialClearanceNm {}\text { nm}$)}{figure.ext.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Three-dimensional fractal geometry control across all evaluated cavity constellations and matched $N=2$ and $N=3$ control families in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} Radial span $R \in [R_{\rm  min}, R_{\rm  max}]$, concentric track/sub-slot count, active rotor tooth planform area $A_{\rm  tooth}$, edge perimeter $P_{\rm  edge}$, disengaged open-slot axial force $F_z(\theta _{\rm  off})$, open-slot area force density $F_z(\theta _{\rm  off})/A_{\rm  tooth}$, open-slot perimeter force density $F_z(\theta _{\rm  off})/P_{\rm  edge}$, and engaged landing-pad axial force $F_z(48^\circ )$ evaluated on the matched \texttt  {Standard} 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM mesh ($656$ panels for $N=0,1$; $1504{}$ panels for $N=2$ and 3-track controls; $3168{}$ panels for 7-track $N=3$ controls; $6{,}784$ panels across four $90^\circ $ sectors for 12-sub-tooth 3D recursive $N=3$ architectures).}}{37}{table.ext.1}\protected@file@percent }
